Shouldn't we indicate that the ValueTask result has been consumed? @stephentoub submitted a PR to do that for historical code: https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/31221

```cs
if (!continueTask.IsCompletedSuccessfully)
{
    return StartTimingReadAwaited(continueTask, readAwaitable, cancellationToken);
}
else
{
    continueTask.GetAwaiter().GetResult();
}
